.ds command sphinx-linklint
.ds COMMAND SPHINX-LINKLINT
.\" ==========
.TH "\*[COMMAND]" 1 "2026-08-04" "sphinx-linklint"
.
.\" ==========
.SH NAME
\*[command] \- check for excessive references in Sphinx documents
.
.\" ==========
.SH SYNOPSIS
.
.SY \*[command]
.RB "[" "\-\-check"
.IR "CHECK" " ["
.BR "," " ... ] ]"
.OP \-\-fix
.I INPUTFILE
[...]
.YS
.
.SY \*[command]
.B \-\-help
.YS
.
.\" ==========
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sphinx-linklint
finds, reports, and optionally removes excessive references from Sphinx source
documents \f[I]INPUTFILE\f[].
.PP
.
.\" ==========
.SH OPTIONS
.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-check\f[] \f[I]CHECK\f[] [ \f[B],\f[] ... ]
Perform only each specified \f[I]CHECK\f[].
The default is \f[B]all\f[].
.
Supported \f[I]CHECK\f[] values are:
.
.RS
.
.TP
.B self
Find references that link to their own section.
For example, in the description of a class, use \f[B]:class:\f[] referring to
itself. These should not be links since they will not take you someplace new.
.
.TP
.B paradup
Find multiple identical references within a single paragraph.
The first should be a link, but subsequent references don't need to be links,
they are just distractions.
.
.TP
.B all
Perform all the above checks.
.
.RE
.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-fix\f[]
Modify each \f[I]INPUTFILE\f[] in place,
correcting the references found by each \f[I]CHECK\f[].
.
The default is to not modify any \f[I]INPUTFILE\f[].
.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help information, then exit.
.
.\" ==========
.SH REPORTING BUGS
.P
Please report any bugs using the
.UR https://github.com/nedbat/sphinx-linklint/issues/new
sphinx-linklint project issue tracker
.UE .
.
